{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/347614-speaking-different-languages-and-compromise","id":347614,"title":"Speaking different languages and compromise","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-22T13:04:52-08:00","id":347614,"title":"Speaking different languages and compromise","content":"Isn't talking in any language apart from your native speech, a little out of character and thus compromise?<br /> <br /> Suppose two demons in Milan (Italy) speak Portoguese to avoid being understood, without any previous indication that they could speak Portoguese. No one heard them anyway. Is it compromise?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or say a Mummy speaks in Hindu and they respond in Hindu. No witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 12-22-2014, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T13:13:38-08:00","id":347636,"title":"","content":"Sure, it can be a little out of character. It's important to remember that there's wiggle room available, in that you risk compromise for actions that are <i>grossly</i> out of character, not just a little out of character. Knowing Portuguese isn't really hugely implausible for somebody in Milan, especially when they may or may not be residents. Translating a message in Egyptian hieroglyphics for your buds you know from AP Calculus class? That's probably a compromise.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd probably also offer differing amounts of wiggle room based on the context of the action \u2014 Cover is, after all, a psychic construct both influencing and influenced by the perceptions of others. It's going to take a grosser contradiction of the identity that forms your Cover when spelunking in a God-Machine facility on your own than it would take when you're interacting with your Cover's close friends and family. There are contradictions so grand that it doesn't matter if nobody ever finds out you did it, but relative strangeness can be hidden away from the world, or exposed by the active observance of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T04:36:45-08:00","id":348184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/347614-speaking-different-languages-and-compromise?p=347636#post347636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, it can be a little out of character. It's important to remember that there's wiggle room available, in that you risk compromise for actions that are <i>grossly</i> out of character, not just a little out of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seriously cannot be overstated enough, both for this specifically and for judging actions that are &quot;out-of-character&quot; for compromise in general. I've said it before, but my personal guideline for &quot;does this cause compromise&quot; is: does witnessing this specific cover take this specific action or portray this specific characteristic cause the average person watching them (or someone specific if someone's actually watching) any measure of cognitive dissonance? If no, don't roll. So the fact that Stuart the Accountant knows Portuguese is an interesting fact, while watching Stuart the Accountant steal the sidearm off a soldier and kill four of them with a shot each before they get a chance to respond is easily a compromise.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T16:29:53-08:00","id":348619,"title":"","content":"So,<br /> <br /> I think you could argue speaking strange languages is often a Cover check. I would not, as it seems to be one of the sort of signature things Demons can do in DtD and almost an iconic ability of the template. It's a neat thing you do in Demon you don't do in other WoD games. Of course, so is go Demon Form which is a compromise, but the linguistic thing is a different sort of ability. But a bus driver from Georgia who has not traveled yet knows Tagalog and Czech is unusual, a best. A globe-trotting playboy not so much.<br /> <br /> It's sort of important to discuss Compromises with your group, I think. The rules are vague, which is not a problem if people are essentially on the same page, but can be if everyone assumes everyone else shares their ideas. The languages thing is a good example...if the GM thinks it is players think it isn't, it can cause issue. Similarly, if players assume it is the GM may wonder why they never use the ability. There are other cases too. What is most important is that the group gets on the same page.<br /> <br /> <br /> But my short answer is &quot;I can see the logic to it, but I wouldn't due to the iconic nature of the mechanic and it's purpose in the campaign&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T22:10:54-08:00","id":351341,"title":"","content":"My players ran into a situation where they captured the Hunter cell pursuing them. Since the Hunters were at least partially informed (the players didn't know <i>how well</i> informed), switching to a different language, even a common one like Spanish, would provide the Hunters with an <i>enormous</i> clue of what they were dealing with; I told them it would be a very troubling development for the future as well as a compromise roll.<br /> <br /> The players worked out other ways to communicate secretly, which made for an interesting interrogation, and then a fun story when both parties were compelled to cooperate... and the players needed to keep finding new ways to shake their temporary allies off the trail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 12-27-2014, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}